'''''Coleus comosus''''', [[Synonym (taxonomy)|synonym]] '''''Plectranthus ornatus''''', is a [[flowering plant]] from the mint family [[Lamiaceae]], native to eastern Africa (Eritrea, Ethiopia, Kenya, Tanzania and Uganda).<ref name=POWO_445949-1/>

A plant sold under the name "''Coleus canina''" or "scaredy cat plant" is supposed to scare off cats and dogs. An attempt to register "''Coleus canina''" to receive [[plant variety (law)|plant variety]] protection failed as it was considered to be only a [[Vegetative reproduction|clone]] of ''Coleus comosus''.<ref name=Wink04/>

